silm:instances_papers_21_ologs_and_typed_english_chapters_03_typed_verb_discipline_sections_04_symmetric_verb_cheese_trap_concrete_anchor_3_tau_V#typedverbgate silm:hasLongDescription "The TypedVerbGate is the gate with inverse-discipline check. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'tau_V', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
